  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "If \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) are positive integers for which \\(2^x 3^y = 1296,\\) what is the value of \\(x + y?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(8\\)",
    "B": "\\(9\\)",
    "C": "\\(10\\)",
    "D": "\\(11\\)",
    "E": "\\(12\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The left side is already expressed using the primes \\(2\\) and \\(3\\), so factor \\(1296\\) into those same primes:\n\\[\n1296=16\\cdot81=2^4 3^4.\n\\]\nPrime factorization is unique, so \\(x=4\\) and \\(y=4\\). Both are positive integers, as required. Therefore \\(x+y=4+4=8\\), choice A.",
